# Netlify's equivalent of the rules in vercel.json, kept in step by hand.
#
# Vercel is what serves plauvia.com and reads vercel.json instead of this file;
# this exists so that a deploy to Netlify behaves the same way rather than
# quietly turning every mistyped address into a copy of the home page, which is
# what the single catch-all rule that used to be here did.

/bg              /              301!
/bg/*            /:splat        301!
/home            /              301!
/homepage        /              301!
/en/home         /en            301!
/en/homepage     /en            301!

# The only addresses that need the shell without having a file of their own.
/app/*           /app/index.html   200

# Everything else that does not exist is a real 404, answered by the branded page.
/*               /404.html      404
